3D-Bausteine holds two programs under two different terms.

1. Version 1.3 of 2002 by Herbert Kleber

   The files of version 1.3 at the root of this repository, the forms
   (*.frm, *.frx), the modules (*.bas), the project files (*.vbp, *.VBW),
   the C source Grafik3d.cpp, the binaries (3D_BAU.EXE, SCREEN.EXE,
   graf3d32.dll), the scene files (*.pov, *.pov.bak), the images (*.bmp)
   and START.BAT, and the project diary in README.md below its first
   rule, carry no license. Every right in them stays with their author,
   Herbert Kleber. Nothing in this repository grants a license to them,
   and the license of version 2.0 below does not reach them.

2. Version 2.0 of 2026 by Florian Kleber

   The rewrite in Rust, every file under crates/, service/, web/, tools/,
   tests/, Documentation/ and .github/, the files Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock,
   rust-toolchain.toml, rustfmt.toml, .gitignore, .gitmodules and this
   file, and the part of README.md above its first rule, is

       Copyright (C) 2026 Florian Kleber

   and licensed under the GNU General Public License version 2 only,
   SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only. The full text stands in
   LICENSES/GPL-2.0-only.txt, which the Free Software Foundation publishes
   under the terms it states itself.

   Every file of version 2.0 whose type has a comment syntax opens with
   its SPDX line, in the comment form of its language: the Rust, WGSL,
   JavaScript, CSS, HTML, SVG, shell, Python, YAML and TOML files, the
   file tests/requirements.txt, and the first cell of every notebook under
   tests/notebooks. The files of version 2.0 whose type has no comment
   syntax, or whose syntax a tool writes, carry no SPDX line and fall
   under this section all the same:

   - the Markdown pages under Documentation/ and the part of README.md
     named above,
   - the JSON files, such as tests/fixtures/parity.json,
   - the lock files Cargo.lock, service/Cargo.lock and
     crates/bausteine-web/Cargo.lock, which cargo writes,
   - the pictures under Documentation/images/ in PNG, which are renders
     of version 2.0 written by the test notebooks,
   - the files .gitignore and .gitmodules, and this file.

   tools/license_lint.py checks the SPDX line of every file of version
   2.0, and tools/lint.sh and the continuous integration run it.

   Version 2.0 implements the design described in the diploma thesis
   "Grundlagen der 3D-Computergrafik" by Herbert Kleber. It contains no
   code of version 1.3.

3. Aosabi

   The submodule third_party/aosabi is Aosabi, under the terms of its own
   LICENSE and NOTICE in that folder.

Documentation/licensing.md says how a change checks that every crate a
build of version 2.0 links is compatible with GPL-2.0-only.
